#: ../../changelog/firmware/v5.0.1.rst:338
msgid ""
"None of this affects MicroPython scripts. ``py_image.c`` was split, with the"
" descriptor objects (cascade, keypoints, LBP, keypoint match) moving to "
"``py_image_descriptor.c`` and the statistics objects (similarity, "
"statistics, percentile, threshold, histogram) to ``py_image_stats.c``. The "
"imlib encoder API was aligned with the rest of imlib: ``jpeg_compress`` / "
"``png_compress`` return ``0`` on success and ``-1`` on error, and "
"``jpeg_compress`` lost its ``realloc`` argument (resizing is gated on buffer"
" ownership). ``OMV_PROTOCOL_MAX_CHANNELS`` became "
"``OMV_PROTOCOL_CHANNEL_MAX`` in ``omv_protocol_channel.h``, and ports now "
"call ``py_protocol_init0()`` on init. The ``OMV_PAG7936_MIPI_CSI2`` board "
"define is gone (the interface is selected at runtime). CI dependency bumps "
"and an empty-release-changelog fix round it out. See the `firmware "
"repository <https://github.com/openmv/openmv>`__ history for fork-relevant "
"detail."
msgstr ""
"Niets hiervan raakt MicroPython-scripts. ``py_image.c`` is opgesplitst, "
"waarbij de descriptor-objecten (cascade, keypoints, LBP, keypoint match) "
"naar ``py_image_descriptor.c`` zijn verhuisd en de statistiekobjecten "
"(similarity, statistics, percentile, threshold, histogram) naar "
"``py_image_stats.c``\\ . De imlib-encoder-API is in lijn gebracht met de "
"rest van imlib: ``jpeg_compress`` / ``png_compress`` retourneren ``0`` bij "
"succes en ``-1`` bij een fout, en ``jpeg_compress`` verloor zijn "
"``realloc``\\ -argument (herdimensioneren hangt af van buffereigendom). "
"``OMV_PROTOCOL_MAX_CHANNELS`` werd ``OMV_PROTOCOL_CHANNEL_MAX`` in "
"``omv_protocol_channel.h``\\ , en ports roepen nu ``py_protocol_init0()`` "
"aan bij init. De board-define ``OMV_PAG7936_MIPI_CSI2`` is verdwenen (de "
"interface wordt tijdens runtime gekozen). CI-dependency-bumps en een fix "
"voor een lege release-changelog maken het af. Zie de geschiedenis van de "
"`firmware-repository <https://github.com/openmv/openmv>`__ voor details die "
"relevant zijn voor forks."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v5.0.1.rst:353
msgid "Migration checklist"
msgstr "Migratiechecklist"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v5.0.1.rst:355
msgid ""
"**Still on** ``import sensor``? It works, with a warning. Move to :mod:`csi`"
" (:ref:`v5.0.0 migration <v5_0_0_s1>`); replace ``disable_delays`` / "
"``disable_full_flush`` with the ``csi.CSI()`` constructor arguments and drop"
" ``get_fb`` / auto-rotation calls."
msgstr ""
"**Nog steeds op** ``import sensor``\\ ? Het werkt, met een waarschuwing. "
"Stap over naar :mod:`csi` (\\ :ref:`v5.0.0-migratie <v5_0_0_s1>`\\ ); "
"vervang ``disable_delays`` / ``disable_full_flush`` door de "
"constructorargumenten van ``csi.CSI()`` en laat ``get_fb``\\ - / auto-"
"rotatie-aanroepen weg."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v5.0.1.rst:359
msgid ""
"**Load a single image with** ``copy_to_fb=True`` **and expect to see it?** "
"Add ``img.flush()`` after loading."
msgstr ""
"**Laad je één enkele afbeelding met** ``copy_to_fb=True`` **en verwacht je "
"die te zien?** Voeg ``img.flush()`` toe na het laden."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v5.0.1.rst:361
msgid ""
"**Copied the YOLOv8 post-processor?** Index the thresholded output by row "
"(``bb[:, 4:]``) rather than by column."
msgstr ""
"**De YOLOv8-post-processor gekopieerd?** Indexeer de gethresholde uitvoer "
"per rij (\\ ``bb[:, 4:]``\\ ) in plaats van per kolom."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v5.0.1.rst:363
msgid ""
"**Compare** ``csi0.framesize()`` **after setting a tuple?** It now returns "
":data:`csi.CUSTOM`."
msgstr ""
"**Vergelijk je** ``csi0.framesize()`` **na het instellen van een tuple?** "
"Die retourneert nu :data:`csi.CUSTOM`\\ ."

